-- Section 160 calls the section 151(b) rule on what stock may be made redeemable (dg3-stock-issue). Out of range: section 243 and 244 (dg5),
-- Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 (the Uniform Commercial Code as enacted in Delaware, not an input).

§ `Section 159: shares of stock; personal property, transfer and taxation`

-- The shares of stock in every corporation are deemed personal property, transferable as provided in Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6.
-- That Article is not an input: whether a transfer is made as it provides is taken as a stated fact.
-- src:524 | The shares of stock in every corporation shall be deemed personal property and transferable as provided in Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6. No stock or bonds issued by any corporation organized under this chapter shall be taxed by this State when the same shall be owned by nonresidents of this State, or by foreign corporations. Whenever any transfer of shares shall be made for collateral security, and not absolutely, it shall be so expressed in the entry of transfer if, when the certificates are presented to the corporation for transfer or uncertificated shares are requested to be transferred, both the transferor and transferee request the corporation to do so.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 159 (src:524)
GIVEN `the property is shares of stock in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 159 the shares are deemed personal property` `the property is shares of stock in a corporation` MEANS
    `the property is shares of stock in a corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 159 (src:524)
GIVEN `the transfer is made as Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 159 the shares are transferable by that transfer` `the transfer is made as Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 provides` MEANS
    `the transfer is made as Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 provides`

-- No stock or bonds issued by a corporation organized under the chapter shall be taxed by this State when owned by nonresidents of this State or by foreign corporations.
-- The section says nothing of stock or bonds owned by anyone else, so that case is NOTHING.
-- src:524 | No stock or bonds issued by any corporation organized under this chapter shall be taxed by this State when the same shall be owned by nonresidents of this State, or by foreign corporations. Whenever any transfer of shares shall be made for collateral security, and not absolutely, it shall be so expressed in the entry of transfer if, when the certificates are presented to the corporation for transfer or uncertificated shares are requested to be transferred, both the transferor and transferee request the corporation to do so.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 159 (src:524)
GIVEN `the stock or bonds were issued by a corporation organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner is a nonresident of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner is a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 159 the stock or bonds are exempt from taxation by this State` `the stock or bonds were issued by a corporation organized under this chapter` `the owner is a nonresident of this State` `the owner is a foreign corporation` MEANS
    IF     `the stock or bonds were issued by a corporation organized under this chapter`
       AND (`the owner is a nonresident of this State` OR `the owner is a foreign corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- When a transfer of shares is made for collateral security, and not absolutely, it shall be so expressed in the entry of transfer if, when the certificates are presented
-- for transfer or uncertificated shares are requested to be transferred, both the transferor and the transferee request the corporation to do so.
-- src:524 | Whenever any transfer of shares shall be made for collateral security, and not absolutely, it shall be so expressed in the entry of transfer if, when the certificates are presented to the corporation for transfer or uncertificated shares are requested to be transferred, both the transferor and transferee request the corporation to do so.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 159 (src:524)
GIVEN `the transfer is made for collateral security and not absolutely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both the transferor and the transferee request the corporation to express that when the certificates are presented or the transfer of uncertificated shares is requested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 159 the entry of transfer must express that the transfer is for collateral security` `the transfer is made for collateral security and not absolutely` `both the transferor and the transferee request the corporation to express that when the certificates are presented or the transfer of uncertificated shares is requested` MEANS
        `the transfer is made for collateral security and not absolutely`
    AND `both the transferor and the transferee request the corporation to express that when the certificates are presented or the transfer of uncertificated shares is requested`

§ `Section 160: corporation's powers respecting ownership, voting, etc., of its own stock; rights of stock called for redemption`

-- The facts about a purchase or redemption of the corporation's own shares for cash or other property, for section 160(a)(1).
-- src:529 | Purchase or redeem its own shares of capital stock for cash or other property when the capital of the corporation is impaired or when such purchase or redemption would cause any impairment of the capital of the corporation, except that a corporation other than a nonstock corporation may purchase or redeem out of capital any of its own shares which are entitled upon any distribution of its assets, whether by dividend or in liquidation, to a preference over another class or series of its stock, or, if no shares entitled to such a preference are outstanding, any of its own shares, if such shares will be retired upon their acquisition and the capital of the corporation reduced in accordance with §§ 243 and 244 of this title. Nothing in this subsection shall invalidate or otherwise affect a note, debenture or other obligation of a corporation given by it as consideration for its acquisition by purchase, redemption or exchange of its shares of stock if at the time such note, debenture or obligation was delivered by the corporation its capital was not then impaired or did not thereby become impaired;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(a)(1) (src:529)
DECLARE `s 160(a)(1) Facts about a purchase or redemption of the corporation's own shares` HAS
    `the kind of corporation`                                                                  IS A `Kind of corporation`
    `the capital of the corporation is impaired`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purchase or redemption would cause an impairment of the capital`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the shares are entitled upon any distribution of assets, by dividend or in liquidation, to a preference over another class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no shares entitled to such a preference are outstanding`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the shares will be retired upon their acquisition`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: sections 243 and 244 (piece dg5): reduction of capital
    `the capital of the corporation is reduced in accordance with sections 243 and 244`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- No corporation shall purchase or redeem its own shares of capital stock for cash or other property when its capital is impaired or the purchase or redemption would impair it,
-- except that a corporation other than a nonstock corporation may purchase or redeem out of capital (1) any of its own shares entitled upon any distribution of assets to a preference over another class or series, or
-- (2) if no shares entitled to such a preference are outstanding, any of its own shares, if the shares will be retired on acquisition and the capital reduced in accordance with sections 243 and 244.
-- The retirement-and-reduction condition is read as qualifying only the second limb, which it follows (Fork F9).
-- src:529 | except that a corporation other than a nonstock corporation may purchase or redeem out of capital any of its own shares which are entitled upon any distribution of its assets, whether by dividend or in liquidation, to a preference over another class or series of its stock, or, if no shares entitled to such a preference are outstanding, any of its own shares, if such shares will be retired upon their acquisition and the capital of the corporation reduced in accordance with §§ 243 and 244 of this title. Nothing in this subsection shall invalidate or otherwise affect a note, debenture or other obligation of a corporation given by it as consideration for its acquisition by purchase, redemption or exchange of its shares of stock if at the time such note, debenture or obligation was delivered by the corporation its capital was not then impaired or did not thereby become impaired;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(a)(1) (src:529)
GIVEN f IS A `s 160(a)(1) Facts about a purchase or redemption of the corporation's own shares`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(a)(1) the purchase or redemption is barred` f MEANS
        (    f's `the capital of the corporation is impaired`
         OR  f's `the purchase or redemption would cause an impairment of the capital`)
    AND (NOT (    (NOT `the kind is a nonstock corporation` (f's `the kind of corporation`))
              AND (    f's `the shares are entitled upon any distribution of assets, by dividend or in liquidation, to a preference over another class or series`
                   OR  (    f's `no shares entitled to such a preference are outstanding`
                        AND f's `the shares will be retired upon their acquisition`
                        AND f's `the capital of the corporation is reduced in accordance with sections 243 and 244`))))

-- Nothing in the subsection invalidates or affects a note, debenture or other obligation given by the corporation as consideration for the acquisition of its shares
-- if at the time it was delivered the capital was not then impaired or did not thereby become impaired. The "or" is kept as written (Fork F8).
-- src:529 | Nothing in this subsection shall invalidate or otherwise affect a note, debenture or other obligation of a corporation given by it as consideration for its acquisition by purchase, redemption or exchange of its shares of stock if at the time such note, debenture or obligation was delivered by the corporation its capital was not then impaired or did not thereby become impaired;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(a)(1) (src:529)
GIVEN `at the time the note, debenture or obligation was delivered the capital was not then impaired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at that time the capital did not thereby become impaired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(a)(1) the note, debenture or obligation given for the acquisition is not invalidated` `at the time the note, debenture or obligation was delivered the capital was not then impaired` `at that time the capital did not thereby become impaired` MEANS
        `at the time the note, debenture or obligation was delivered the capital was not then impaired`
    OR  `at that time the capital did not thereby become impaired`

-- Section 160(a)(2): no corporation shall purchase, for more than the price at which they may then be redeemed, any of its shares that are redeemable at the option of the corporation.
-- src:530 | Purchase, for more than the price at which they may then be redeemed, any of its shares which are redeemable at the option of the corporation; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(a)(2) (src:530)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemable at the option of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price the corporation would pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the price at which the shares may then be redeemed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(a)(2) the purchase is barred` `the shares are redeemable at the option of the corporation` `the price the corporation would pay` `the price at which the shares may then be redeemed` MEANS
        `the shares are redeemable at the option of the corporation`
    AND (`the price the corporation would pay` GREATER THAN `the price at which the shares may then be redeemed`)

-- Section 160(a)(3): a corporation other than a nonstock corporation shall not redeem any of its shares unless the redemption is authorised by section 151(b) and then only in accordance with that section
-- and the certificate of incorporation; a nonstock corporation shall not redeem any of its membership interests unless the redemption is authorised by the certificate and then only in accordance with it.
-- src:531 | In the case of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation, redeem any of its shares, unless their redemption is authorized by § 151(b) of this title and then only in accordance with such section and the certificate of incorporation, or
-- src:532 | In the case of a nonstock corporation, redeem any of its membership interests, unless their redemption is authorized by the certificate of incorporation and then only in accordance with the certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(a)(3) (src:531-532)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of corporation`
      r IS A `s 151(b) Redemption terms`
      `the redemption is made in accordance with section 151(b) and the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation authorises the redemption of the membership interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the redemption of the membership interests is made in accordance with the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(a)(3) the redemption is barred` k r `the redemption is made in accordance with section 151(b) and the certificate of incorporation` `the certificate of incorporation authorises the redemption of the membership interests` `the redemption of the membership interests is made in accordance with the certificate of incorporation` MEANS
    NOT (IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` k
         THEN (    `the certificate of incorporation authorises the redemption of the membership interests`
               AND `the redemption of the membership interests is made in accordance with the certificate of incorporation`)
         ELSE (    `s 151(b) the stock may be made subject to redemption` r
               AND `the redemption is made in accordance with section 151(b) and the certificate of incorporation`))

-- Section 160(a), the grant: every corporation may purchase, redeem, receive, take or otherwise acquire, own and hold, sell, lend, exchange, transfer or otherwise dispose of, pledge, use and otherwise deal in and with its own shares,
-- provided that none of the three bars in paragraphs (1) to (3) applies. This rule takes the outcome of each bar as a plain input; the bars themselves are the three rules above.
-- src:528 | Every corporation may purchase, redeem, receive, take or otherwise acquire, own and hold, sell, lend, exchange, transfer or otherwise dispose of, pledge, use and otherwise deal in and with its own shares …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(a) (src:528)
GIVEN `the purchase or redemption is barred by paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is barred by paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the redemption is barred by paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(a) the corporation may deal in its own shares` `the purchase or redemption is barred by paragraph (1)` `the purchase is barred by paragraph (2)` `the redemption is barred by paragraph (3)` MEANS
    NOT (    `the purchase or redemption is barred by paragraph (1)`
          OR `the purchase is barred by paragraph (2)`
          OR `the redemption is barred by paragraph (3)`)

-- Section 160(b): nothing in the section limits or affects the corporation's right to resell, under section 153(c), any of its shares purchased or redeemed out of surplus
-- that have not been, and are not required by the certificate of incorporation to be, retired.
-- src:533 | Nothing in this section limits or affects a corporation’s right to resell, under § 153(c) of this title, any of its shares theretofore purchased or redeemed out of surplus and which have not been, or are not required by the certificate of incorporation to be, retired.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(b) (src:533)
GIVEN `the shares were purchased or redeemed out of surplus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares have been retired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation requires the shares to be retired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(b) the corporation's right to resell the shares under section 153(c) is unaffected` `the shares were purchased or redeemed out of surplus` `the shares have been retired` `the certificate of incorporation requires the shares to be retired` MEANS
        `the shares were purchased or redeemed out of surplus`
    AND (NOT `the shares have been retired`)
    AND (NOT `the certificate of incorporation requires the shares to be retired`)

-- Section 160(c): shares of a corporation's capital stock neither vote nor count for quorum purposes if they belong to (1) the corporation; (2) another corporation, if a majority of the shares entitled to vote
-- in the election of its directors is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation; or (3) any other entity, if a majority of its voting power is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation
-- or it is otherwise controlled, directly or indirectly, by the corporation.
-- src:534 | Shares of a corporation’s capital stock shall neither be entitled to vote nor be counted for quorum purposes if such shares belong to:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(c) (src:534)
DECLARE `s 160(c) Who holds the shares` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation itself under s 160(c)`
    `another corporation under s 160(c)`
    `any other entity under s 160(c)`
    `a holder that is neither the corporation, a corporation it controls nor an entity it controls under s 160(c)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(c) (src:534-538)
DECLARE `s 160(c) Facts about shares of the corporation's capital stock` HAS
    `who holds the shares` IS A `s 160(c) Who holds the shares`
    `a majority of the shares entitled to vote in the election of directors of the other corporation is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a majority of the voting power of the other entity is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other entity is otherwise controlled, directly or indirectly, by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder holds the shares in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:535 | (1) The corporation;
-- src:536 | (2) Another corporation, if a majority of the shares entitled to vote in the election of directors of such other corporation is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation; or
-- src:537 | (3) Any other entity, if a majority of the voting power of such other entity is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation or if such other entity is otherwise controlled, directly or indirectly, by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(c) (src:534-537)
GIVEN f IS A `s 160(c) Facts about shares of the corporation's capital stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(c) the shares neither vote nor count for quorum purposes` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `who holds the shares`
    WHEN `the corporation itself under s 160(c)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another corporation under s 160(c)` THEN f's `a majority of the shares entitled to vote in the election of directors of the other corporation is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation`
    WHEN `any other entity under s 160(c)` THEN
            (    f's `a majority of the voting power of the other entity is held, directly or indirectly, by the corporation`
             OR  f's `the other entity is otherwise controlled, directly or indirectly, by the corporation`)
    WHEN `a holder that is neither the corporation, a corporation it controls nor an entity it controls under s 160(c)` THEN FALSE

-- Nothing in the section limits the right of any corporation to vote stock, including its own stock, held by it in a fiduciary capacity.
-- src:538 | Nothing in this section shall be construed as limiting the right of any corporation to vote stock, including but not limited to its own stock, held by it in a fiduciary capacity.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(c) (src:538)
GIVEN f IS A `s 160(c) Facts about shares of the corporation's capital stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(c) the section does not limit the holder's right to vote the stock` f MEANS
    f's `the holder holds the shares in a fiduciary capacity`

-- What the section settles about voting: shares that belong to the corporation or an entity it controls do not vote, unless held in a fiduciary capacity, in which case the right to vote is preserved.
-- The fiduciary clause speaks of voting only. It neither restores the shares to the quorum count nor confirms that they stay out of it, so for quorum purposes the answer is NOTHING when the clause applies (Fork F19).
-- Any other case is NOTHING, because this section does not say who is entitled to vote (that is for the sections on voting).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(c) (src:534-538)
GIVEN f IS A `s 160(c) Facts about shares of the corporation's capital stock`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(c) the shares may be voted, as far as this section decides` f MEANS
    IF `s 160(c) the section does not limit the holder's right to vote the stock` f
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `s 160(c) the shares neither vote nor count for quorum purposes` f
          THEN JUST FALSE
          ELSE NOTHING)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(c) (src:534-538)
GIVEN f IS A `s 160(c) Facts about shares of the corporation's capital stock`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(c) the shares are counted for quorum purposes, as far as this section decides` f MEANS
    IF `s 160(c) the shares neither vote nor count for quorum purposes` f
    THEN (IF `s 160(c) the section does not limit the holder's right to vote the stock` f
          THEN NOTHING
          ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 160(d): shares called for redemption are not deemed outstanding for voting, or for determining the total number of shares entitled to vote on any matter,
-- on and after the date on which notice of redemption has been sent to holders and a sum sufficient to redeem the shares has been irrevocably deposited or set aside.
-- From the later of those two dates.
-- src:539 | Shares which have been called for redemption shall not be deemed to be outstanding shares for the purpose of voting or determining the total number of shares entitled to vote on any matter on and after the date on which notice of redemption has been sent to holders thereof and a sum sufficient to redeem such shares has been irrevocably deposited or set aside to pay the redemption price to the holders of the shares upon surrender of certificates therefor.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 160(d) (src:539)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day notice of redemption was sent to the holders, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day a sum sufficient to redeem the shares was irrevocably deposited or set aside, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160(d) the shares called for redemption are not outstanding for voting on the day` day `the day notice of redemption was sent to the holders, if it was` `the day a sum sufficient to redeem the shares was irrevocably deposited or set aside, if it was` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day notice of redemption was sent to the holders, if it was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST sent THEN
        CONSIDER `the day a sum sufficient to redeem the shares was irrevocably deposited or set aside, if it was`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST deposited THEN
            day AT LEAST (IF sent AT LEAST deposited THEN sent ELSE deposited)

§ `Section 169: situs of ownership of stock`

-- The purposes for which the section speaks of the situs of the ownership of stock.
-- src:583 | For all purposes of title, action, attachment, garnishment and jurisdiction of all courts held in this State, but not for the purpose of taxation, the situs of the ownership of the capital stock of all corporations existing under the laws of this State, whether organized under this chapter or otherwise, shall be regarded as in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 169 (src:583)
DECLARE `s 169 The purpose for which the situs of the ownership of stock is asked about` IS ONE OF
    `title under s 169`
    `action under s 169`
    `attachment under s 169`
    `garnishment under s 169`
    `jurisdiction of the courts held in this State under s 169`
    `taxation under s 169`
    `another purpose under s 169`

-- For all purposes of title, action, attachment, garnishment and jurisdiction of all courts held in this State, but not for the purpose of taxation,
-- the situs of the ownership of the capital stock of all corporations existing under the laws of this State, organized under the chapter or otherwise, is regarded as in this State.
-- For taxation the section says the situs is not so regarded; for another purpose it says nothing: NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 169 (src:583)
GIVEN `the corporation exists under the laws of this State, whether organized under this chapter or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 169 The purpose for which the situs of the ownership of stock is asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169 the situs of the ownership of the capital stock is regarded as in this State` `the corporation exists under the laws of this State, whether organized under this chapter or otherwise` purpose MEANS
    IF `the corporation exists under the laws of this State, whether organized under this chapter or otherwise`
    THEN (CONSIDER purpose
          WHEN `taxation under s 169` THEN JUST FALSE
          WHEN `another purpose under s 169` THEN NOTHING
          OTHERWISE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING
